---
/*
  /{slug} — a constellation's canonical page: landed inside the suite.
  Root-level slugs by design: sharing is a core use (vision.md §5) and
  `/conditions-not-character` is the prettiest URL for it. Static routes
  (/blog, /about, …) always win over this dynamic one.

  An unknown slug drifts home (the overview) rather than a hard 404 — a
  mistyped star is a curiosity, and the overview is the kindest place to land.
*/
import SiteLayout from '../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';
import ConstellationSuite from '../components/ConstellationSuite.astro';
import { getConstellation } from '../lib/constellations';
import { toPlainText } from '../lib/markdown';

const supabase = Astro.locals.supabase;
const { slug = '' } = Astro.params;

const constellation = await getConstellation(supabase, slug);
if (!constellation || constellation.items.length === 0) {
  return Astro.redirect('/', 302);
}

/*
  ⚠⚠ THE CACHE HEADER BRANCHES, AND THE BRANCH IS THE WHOLE PIECE (24 · Piece 3).

  This route DOUBLES AS THE DRAFT PREVIEW — see `getConstellation`, and the note
  at the top of this file: a draft is RLS-hidden from anon, so reaching one here
  means the viewer is Michael. Setting `s-maxage` unconditionally would therefore
  push an UNPUBLISHED constellation into the public CDN and serve it to everyone
  for a minute. That is not a hypothetical; it is what the header does.

  ⚠ THE TEST IS NEGATIVE — `!== 'published'`, not `=== 'draft'` — and
  `blog/[slug].astro` states why in the same words: *"One rule, so a tier added
  later can't quietly fall through to the public cache branch."* A third status
  invented in a year is private by default rather than public by accident.

  ⚠ AND `/` NEEDS NO SUCH BRANCH, which looks like an inconsistency and is two
  different correct answers. `listConstellations` filters to `status =
  'published'` for EVERY viewer, admin included, and says so — the overview is
  the public truth by construction, so there is nothing there to leak.
*/
if (constellation.status !== 'published') {
  Astro.response.headers.set('Cache-Control', 'private, no-store');
} else {
  Astro.response.headers.set('Cache-Control', 'public, s-maxage=60, stale-while-revalidate=86400');
}
---

{
  /* `toPlainText` on the description — it is Markdown (2026-08-11) and it lands
    in <meta name="description"> and og:description. A search result or a link
    preview reading "**wayfinding** — for yourself" is the marks outliving the
    one surface that knows how to render them. */
}
<SiteLayout
  title={constellation.name}
  description={toPlainText(constellation.description) || undefined}
  active="home"
  backToTop={false}
>
  <ConstellationSuite constellation={constellation} />
</SiteLayout>
